    "description": "An armchair, stool and service table made from lightweight polystyrene bodies wrapped in polyester bandage soaked in synthetic resin. The bandage hardens in minutes, turning a fragile foam shape into structural furniture — the same principle as a plaster cast on a broken bone. The wrapping is visible: the textile surface, with its overlapping layers and rough edges, becomes the finish. Available in red, pink and black. First developed self-initiated in 2006, then selected by Cappellini for their Collezione.",
    "significance": "Hans borrows a medical repair technique and makes it a manufacturing process. The name ‘Fracture’ is literal — the furniture looks like it’s been bandaged. But the bandage isn’t healing a break, it’s creating the strength. The process that usually fixes damaged objects is here the process that makes new ones. It also produces furniture with a textile character — the polyester wrapping gives it a woven surface that no injection mould or CNC router could achieve.",
