        "reason": "Rebecca Crompton's embroidered tray cloth (1930s) uses thread to make pictures — textile as image. Anni Albers's Wall Hanging (1926) uses thread to make systems — textile as structure. Crompton's needle draws; Albers's loom computes. Two women, two arguments about what thread is for."
