        "reason": "Piano and Rogers' Pompidou (1977) puts everything on the outside — structure, services, colour, spectacle. Ando's Church of the Light (1989) puts everything on the inside — light, silence, absence, contemplation. Two buildings that make opposite arguments about what architecture should show the world."
