        "reason": "Vignelli's New York Subway signage (1970) creates transit identity through systematic typography — Helvetica at every station, consistency as recognition. Guimard's Métro entrances (1900) create transit identity through organic sculpture — iron plants at every station, uniqueness as recognition. Two solutions to the same problem — how do you brand an underground railway? — separated by seventy years and opposite aesthetics."
