    "significance": "Studio Job detonated the boundary between furniture, sculpture, and commentary. Robber Baron treats the history of industrial capitalism as decorative programme — smokestacks and skulls cast in gold, excess critiquing excess. It launched the 'collectible design' market that would dominate design fairs for the next decade, and proved that furniture could carry political content without being didactic.",
