        "id": 688,
        "type": "zeitgeist",
        "reason": "Lacaton & Vassal's Palais de Tokyo (2012) achieves maximum space through minimum means — subtraction as method. BIG's VIA 57 West (2016) achieves maximum amenity through maximum form — hybridisation as method. Two Pritzker-recognised practices with opposite temperaments: one removes, the other combines."
