    "description": "A blossoming tree sculpture that produces ephemeral flowers made of mist. Each blossom is a smoke-filled bubble released from bronze branches — when touched, the bubble bursts and releases a scented fog that disappears in seconds. The mist is generated from recycled water; the scent references flowers associated with each city where the installation travels. Commissioned by COS for Milan Design Week 2017, it was the most photographed installation of the year.",
    "significance": "Studio Swine designed an object whose product is its own disappearance. New Spring creates beauty that lasts seconds — the opposite of design's usual ambition for permanence. The smoke blossoms cannot be collected, stored, or resold. They exist only in the moment of contact between hand and bubble. It argues that the most memorable designed experience might be the one that leaves no physical trace.",
