    "description": "A single-piece magnesium-alloy chair cast using the same manufacturing process as laptop housings and automotive parts — die-cast in one shot, 2.5kg total weight, stackable to twenty. The form derives from natural branching structures: the legs spread like roots, the back curves like a spine, every surface is thinned to the minimum material needed to support load. It was the first single-piece die-cast metal chair in production.",
