    "wikiTitle": null,
    "description": "A polypropylene chair made from a single injection-moulded piece, designed to look handmade. The surface carries deliberate imperfections — drips, sags, and rough edges that mimic wax casting rather than precision moulding. The chair costs under €100 and is fully recyclable. Seymour designed it by hand-modelling the original in wax over a steel armature, then scanning the wax model — transferring handmade irregularity into industrial production.",
