    "movement": "Democratic Luxury",
    "wikiTitle": "Louis_Ghost",
    "description": "A transparent polycarbonate armchair injection-moulded in a single piece, its form an exact replica of a Louis XVI medallion-back chair — oval back, curved arms, tapered legs, every historical proportion preserved. The chair is fully transparent, UV-resistant, and stackable to six. It weighs 6.7kg. Starck's proposition: a chair that has existed since the 18th century, now made from a material that didn't exist until the 20th, sold at a price the 21st century can afford.",
    "significance": "The Louis Ghost is the most commercially successful single chair in contemporary design history — over 1.5 million units sold. It proves that a historical form, emptied of its material, can become radically new. The chair is simultaneously antique and contemporary, ornamental and minimal, expensive-looking and affordable. Starck solved a problem no one thought to articulate: what if you could own a Louis XVI chair for €200?",
