        "type": "method",
        "reason": "Oxman's Silk Pavilion (2013) uses silkworms to fabricate architectural structures — living organisms as manufacturing agents. Lee's Biocouture (2014) uses bacteria to fabricate garment materials — living organisms as manufacturing agents. Both surrender manufacturing control to biology; one builds at architectural scale, the other at textile scale."
