    "description": "A kinetic chandelier whose silk shades open and close like flowers over the course of hours, driven by silent motors and algorithms modelled on the nyctinastic movement of real flowers — the opening and closing triggered by light changes. Each shade is hand-sewn from multiple layers of silk that fold along precisely calculated crease lines. The choreography is different for each installation: the Rijksmuseum version moves in response to daylight entering through the building's glass ceiling.",
